{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act criminal record screening limits","requirement":"A housing provider may not inquire about or consider an applicant's criminal record before making a conditional offer; afterwards it may consider only certain first-, second-, third- or fourth-degree convictions within one to six years, after an individualized assessment.","key_value":"No criminal-record inquiry before a conditional offer","coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent by a housing provider; excludes dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Excludes dwelling units in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units"},"exemptions":"Dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units are excluded from \"rental dwelling unit.\" Federally assisted housing may consider methamphetamine manufacturing convictions and lifetime sex-offender registrants.","penalty":"Director may impose up to $1,000 (no prior violation in five years), $5,000 (one prior) or $10,000 (two or more priors in seven years), and may order cease-and-desist, compliance reporting, a conditional offer or unit, return of the application fee, and up to $1,000 paid to the applicant.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-55","quoted_span":"A housing provider shall not require an applicant to complete any housing application that includes any inquiries regarding an applicant’s criminal record prior to the provision of a conditional offer","interaction":"Does not affect rights or actions existing independently, including under P.L.1945, c.169 (C.10:5-1 et seq.).","confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act application fee disclosure and refund","requirement":"Before accepting an application fee, a housing provider must disclose in writing whether it reviews criminal history and that the applicant may submit evidence of inaccuracies, rehabilitation or mitigating factors; the director may order the fee returned.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent by a housing provider; excludes dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Excludes dwelling units in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units"},"exemptions":"Dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units are excluded from \"rental dwelling unit.\"","penalty":"Unless housing is provided to the applicant, the director may require that the applicant's rental application fee be returned.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-55","quoted_span":"Prior to accepting any application fee, a housing provider shall disclose in writing to the applicant: (1) Whether the eligibility criteria of the housing provider include the review and consideration of criminal history","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act eviction of a reinstated applicant after a successful appeal","requirement":"If a housing provider's appeal succeeds and overturns a director's order that housed the applicant, the provider may evict that former applicant with at least 45 days' notice.","key_value":"45 days' notice","coverage_conditions":"Former applicants residing in a rental dwelling unit as the result of a director's order under this act, where the housing provider later succeeds on appeal.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Applies only to a former applicant housed by a director's order that is overturned on the provider's appeal"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-63","quoted_span":"a determination that the housing provider did not violate the provisions of this act as evidenced by such successful appeal shall be grounds for the housing provider to evict the former applicant if that person resides in a rental dwelling unit owned by the housing provider as the result of the director’s order, so long as the housing provider provides the applicant with at least 45 days’ notice prior to the eviction","interaction":"Notwithstanding any provision of the Anti-Eviction Act, P.L.1974, c.49 (C.2A:18-61.1 et seq.).","confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
